+        // Explicitly disabling echoCancellation/noiseSuppression/
+        // autoGainControl (browsers default all three to true when audio is
+        // just `true`/omitted) — a real trained ML classifier expects
+        // consistent, minimally-processed audio matching what it was
+        // trained on, not audio run through adaptive VoIP-style processing
+        // tuned for human conversational clarity. autoGainControl in
+        // particular re-converges from a neutral starting gain on every
+        // fresh getUserMedia() call (i.e. every start()), so a wake word
+        // spoken in the first moment or so of a newly (re)armed listener —
+        // exactly when a user naturally expects the mic to already be
+        // "ready" — can land at a very different effective level than one
+        // spoken once AGC has settled, even at genuinely identical physical
+        // volume. Confirmed as the likely explanation for wake-word scores
+        // swinging from ~0.01 to ~0.6 attempt-to-attempt at reportedly
+        // consistent input levels.
         this._mediaStream = await navigator.mediaDevices.getUserMedia({
